{
  "name": "counted",
  "note": "Fourth fixture of the conformance corpus (2026-07-30). NEUTRAL GROUND: belongs to neither twin's directory. Covers the COUNTED FOLD — a key's value folded from delta-beats, never stored — and its two derived reads (section placement, provenance). Laid down because scher-pages/src/counted.ts (TS) and scher-core/src/counted.rs (Rust) implement the same operation, and scher-state/src/lib.rs rasterizes a third variant of it; two hand-kept twins drift, which is the problem scher-core-wasm exists to end. Rows are laid verbatim via the one write (lay), so any harness in any language replays them with its own bare lay and gets byte-identical state. THE SHAPE: a delta beat is `count-<holder>-<key>-<n>` whose CONTENT IS THE DELTA as a decimal string (self-describing: the fold never consults a second place), with a bare edge onto the key. A placement beat is `place-<holder>-<key>-<n>` whose content is the section name. Occlusion of a delta beat is how UNDO works — there is no undo stack; the occluded delta simply stops counting, and every downstream read re-folds. NOTE A LIVE DIVERGENCE this corpus is meant to catch: the Rust EventRow calls the headline field `name`, the TS one calls it `title`. Neither was renamed; the wasm boundary reconciles them in one place (see CountedOut in scher-core-wasm/src/lib.rs). If a future port silently picks one spelling, this fixture's `label` expectations go red.",
  "societies": [
    {
      "id": "simple-fold",
      "note": "The base case: deltas fold, including negatives. Value is NEVER stored.",
      "rows": [
        {
          "slug": "lamp",
          "content": "a lamp",
          "name": "Lamp",
          "witnessed": 1
        },
        {
          "slug": "count-moth-lamp-0",
          "content": "3",
          "laid_by": "gran",
          "witnessed": 2
        },
        {
          "slug": "count-moth-lamp-0~c",
          "content": "+3 lamp",
          "subject": "count-moth-lamp-0",
          "object": "lamp",
          "witnessed": 2
        },
        {
          "slug": "count-moth-lamp-1",
          "content": "-1",
          "laid_by": "gran",
          "witnessed": 3
        },
        {
          "slug": "count-moth-lamp-1~c",
          "content": "-1 lamp",
          "subject": "count-moth-lamp-1",
          "object": "lamp",
          "witnessed": 3
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "valueOf": {
          "holder": "moth",
          "key": "lamp",
          "value": 2
        },
        "label": "Lamp",
        "contributions": 2
      }
    },
